WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.230
In Niger, nearly half of all the
people are children under 15.

2
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.380
In Japan, about 3 in every
10 people are 65 or over.

3
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.250
Each year, Niger has far
more births than deaths.

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.600
Japan has more deaths than births,

5
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.850
so its population is shrinking.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.280
So why might a country with too few young

7
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.790
people worry just as much
as one with too many?

8
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:29.030
In this mission, you'll see what
makes a population grow or shrink:

9
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.710
births, deaths and migration.

10
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.090
Then you'll find the population size
that gives the highest output per head,

11
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.050
and see why it can move.

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.180
Your mission: explain
how the size and the age

13
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.120
mix of a population
shape a country's future.
